  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "review: imperatives, questions, there is/are",
      "title_form": "Repaso: imperativos, preguntas y there is/are",
      "title_target": "Review: Imperatives, Questions, and There is/are",
      "description_md_form": "En esta lección repasamos tres estructuras clave para situaciones cotidianas:\n\n**1. Imperativos** para dar direcciones: *Turn left at the hospital.* (Gira a la izquierda en el hospital).\n\n**2. Preguntas** con *do/does* para hablar de síntomas: *Does your head hurt?* (¿Te duele la cabeza?).\n\n**3. There is/are** para indicar existencia: *Is there a doctor here?* (¿Hay un doctor aquí?).\n\nEstas estructuras te ayudan a pedir ayuda y dar indicaciones en inglés. Practica combinándolas: primero pregunta, luego da la instrucción.",
      "description_md_target": "In this lesson we review three key structures for everyday situations:\n\n**1. Imperatives** to give directions: *Turn left at the hospital.*\n\n**2. Questions** with *do/does* to talk about symptoms: *Does your head hurt?*\n\n**3. There is/are** to indicate existence: *Is there a doctor here?*\n\nThese structures help you ask for help and give directions in English. Practice combining them: first ask, then give the instruction.",
      "grammar_structure": "Imperative: Verb + complement | Question: Do/Does + subject + verb? | There is/are: Is/Are there + noun?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "there_is_are",
        "headers": [
          "Forma",
          "Uso",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "There is",
            "Singular",
            "There is a doctor."
          ],
          [
            "There are",
            "Plural",
            "There are two hospitals."
          ],
          [
            "Is there...?",
            "Pregunta singular",
            "Is there a bank?"
          ],
          [
            "Are there...?",
            "Pregunta plural",
            "Are there any doctors?"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "examples": [
        {
